1
00:00:43,563 --> 00:00:45,870
[One Meal with Ha Ru: A Chef's Kitchen]

2
00:00:47,757 --> 00:00:50,807
And that's today's meal, complete.

3
00:00:50,807 --> 00:00:53,464
Today's guest, Yoon Ha Na...

4
00:01:21,417 --> 00:01:22,603
[One Meal with Ha Ru: A Chef's Kitchen]

5
00:01:25,426 --> 00:01:28,577
<i>I'm in Ha Ru's body again?</i>

6
00:01:28,577 --> 00:01:30,632
<i>What is going on this time?</i>

7
00:01:30,632 --> 00:01:32,503
[Episode 8]

8
00:01:32,503 --> 00:01:34,334
Good, very good!

9
00:01:34,334 --> 00:01:35,731
Come on, give it more! Good.

10
00:01:35,731 --> 00:01:37,889
One, two... there.

11
00:01:37,889 --> 00:01:39,466
Smile! Keep that smile shining. Good.

12
00:01:39,466 --> 00:01:41,123
Good, one, two...

13
00:01:41,123 --> 00:01:42,823
One more time.

14
00:01:47,037 --> 00:01:49,153
Good, now look over here.

15
00:01:49,153 --> 00:01:51,103
Twist your arm and bring
the product closer to your face.

16
00:01:51,103 --> 00:01:53,061
Yeah, that's perfect. Right, one, two.

17
00:01:53,061 --> 00:01:55,419
Smile a little for us, good.

18
00:01:57,131 --> 00:01:58,717
Look at the camera. Okay, good.

19
00:01:58,717 --> 00:02:00,369
One more.

20
00:02:02,263 --> 00:02:04,663
Perfect. That's a good shot.

21
00:02:06,777 --> 00:02:09,142
One more. Good. One, two...

22
00:02:11,317 --> 00:02:13,644
Last one. One, two...

23
00:02:13,644 --> 00:02:15,370
Camera. Smile.

24
00:02:15,370 --> 00:02:16,962
Finishing shot.

25
00:02:17,571 --> 00:02:19,954
You can't talk about actor Jung Woo Jae

26
00:02:19,954 --> 00:02:22,594
without mentioning his
debut short film, "That Summer, Us."

27
00:02:22,594 --> 00:02:26,150
The monster new star who suddenly appeared
in Chungmuro, Jung Woo Jae.

28
00:02:26,150 --> 00:02:29,597
The fiery eyes that seemed to
pop out of the screen

29
00:02:29,597 --> 00:02:31,377
still remain the center of attention.

30
00:02:31,377 --> 00:02:35,604
Yes, "That Summer, Us," is a film
that has truly changed my life.

31
00:02:35,604 --> 00:02:39,274
It's all thanks to it that
I'm still so loved by you all.

32
00:02:39,274 --> 00:02:43,536
Yes, your appearance with actress
Yoon Ha Na sure brought a lot of attention.

33
00:02:43,536 --> 00:02:45,771
But ever since your debut...

34
00:02:45,771 --> 00:02:50,597
- you two haven't worked together again.
- Ah, well.

35
00:02:50,597 --> 00:02:52,684
It's a shame, but that's just how it is.

36
00:02:52,684 --> 00:02:56,041
Could we hope for something
to happen in the future?

37
00:03:01,193 --> 00:03:04,037
- I can't say for sure.
- Well, the fans are hoping...

38
00:03:04,037 --> 00:03:09,263
that you have retained that chemistry
we saw from "That Summer, Us" in real life.

39
00:03:09,263 --> 00:03:11,034
A sort of fantasy, if you will.

40
00:03:11,034 --> 00:03:13,503
How are you two faring in real life?

41
00:03:17,537 --> 00:03:22,185
Yoon Ha Na has been
a very good childhood friend of mine.

42
00:03:22,783 --> 00:03:24,590
Now, she is a good colleague,

43
00:03:24,590 --> 00:03:26,990
and a good actress.

44
00:03:26,990 --> 00:03:28,303
Yeah.

45
00:03:29,510 --> 00:03:30,903
[One Meal with Ha Ru: One and Only Table]

46
00:03:35,977 --> 00:03:37,637
[Concept]
[We focus more on people's stories than food]

47
00:03:42,970 --> 00:03:45,050
You came all the way
to the set to show me this?

48
00:03:45,050 --> 00:03:48,121
Well, not just this.

49
00:03:48,121 --> 00:03:49,177
I'm the CEO.

50
00:03:49,177 --> 00:03:52,883
I just wanted to know if you had
any troubles worth mentioning on the set.

51
00:03:52,883 --> 00:03:55,335
I'm here for you, you know!

52
00:03:56,346 --> 00:03:58,903
Come, now, hear me out.

53
00:03:58,903 --> 00:04:00,364
Wow, would you look at that!

54
00:04:00,364 --> 00:04:03,228
Isn't that such an awesome concept?

55
00:04:03,228 --> 00:04:09,178
See, "One Meal with Ha Ru" got so popular
that the channel wants to go full throttle!

56
00:04:09,178 --> 00:04:13,054
The two siblings, Yoon Ha Ru and Yoon Ha Na,
go to a special location in their hometown,

57
00:04:13,054 --> 00:04:16,884
and invite just one special viewer
to share a special meal.

58
00:04:16,884 --> 00:04:19,067
Like a secret restaurant, see?

59
00:04:19,067 --> 00:04:20,585
Doesn't that sound awesome?

60
00:04:20,585 --> 00:04:22,661
Why are you showing me this?

61
00:04:24,450 --> 00:04:28,776
- If you could be their first guest...
- No.

62
00:04:29,803 --> 00:04:33,294
It's nothing hard!
Just cook and serve with them.

63
00:04:33,294 --> 00:04:35,070
Easy breezy. Rest your mind.

64
00:04:35,070 --> 00:04:37,749
Just have a natural conversation
and an overall fun time!

65
00:04:38,923 --> 00:04:40,454
Easy?

66
00:04:41,863 --> 00:04:44,502
Get someone else to do it for you.
I can't do it.

67
00:04:44,502 --> 00:04:46,430
Jung Woo Jae!

68
00:04:46,430 --> 00:04:48,974
Ha Ru is at the peak of his popularity!

69
00:04:48,974 --> 00:04:50,674
And Ha Na, as well...

70
00:04:52,123 --> 00:04:56,734
Well, appearing in a reality show
would really do some good for her.

71
00:04:56,734 --> 00:04:58,643
Hey, Jung Woo Jae, you...

72
00:04:59,246 --> 00:05:01,583
Come on, just be the wind
in their sail, please!

73
00:05:01,583 --> 00:05:04,271
Ye Rang. I'm not doing it.

74
00:05:04,271 --> 00:05:05,894
I'm telling you.

75
00:05:11,257 --> 00:05:12,957
You're still...

76
00:05:14,177 --> 00:05:16,089
not over it, are you?

77
00:05:17,883 --> 00:05:19,875
What, me?

78
00:05:19,875 --> 00:05:22,598
Not you. Ha Ru.

79
00:05:22,598 --> 00:05:25,424
Ha Na, you were just today's guest.

80
00:05:26,817 --> 00:05:28,855
You're so popular right now,

81
00:05:28,855 --> 00:05:33,091
advertisers are dying to get product placement
on "One Meal with Ha Ru."

82
00:05:33,091 --> 00:05:35,009
That's why we're launching the spin-off,

83
00:05:35,009 --> 00:05:39,130
"One and Only Table," right away.

84
00:05:39,130 --> 00:05:40,690
"One and Only Table?"

85
00:05:40,690 --> 00:05:42,860
- What's that?
- Sorry?

86
00:05:43,969 --> 00:05:45,577
Hey.

87
00:05:45,577 --> 00:05:47,447
Why are you looking at me like that?

88
00:05:47,447 --> 00:05:51,481
You're not having second thoughts, are you?

89
00:05:52,821 --> 00:05:54,521
No way.

90
00:06:17,064 --> 00:06:20,797
[Lost Time]

91
00:06:28,377 --> 00:06:31,645
Wow. Guess he's a top star now.

92
00:06:31,645 --> 00:06:35,818
Yeah. He must've worked really hard.

93
00:06:36,411 --> 00:06:38,527
Look, just amazing.

94
00:06:38,527 --> 00:06:40,452
Are you that satisfied with it?

95
00:06:41,135 --> 00:06:42,712
You're here.

96
00:06:42,712 --> 00:06:44,676
Boss!

97
00:06:45,321 --> 00:06:48,195
What's with you?
We talked on the phone yesterday.

98
00:06:56,821 --> 00:06:58,803
- Woo Jae!
- Woo Jae!

99
00:07:00,641 --> 00:07:05,755
Oh, I thought you'd go straight there
after you finished.

100
00:07:07,868 --> 00:07:10,535
I had to drop off some of the crew first.

101
00:07:10,535 --> 00:07:12,005
Woo Jae!

102
00:07:12,628 --> 00:07:15,272
Wow, Jung Woo Jae!

103
00:07:15,272 --> 00:07:16,804
Look at you!

104
00:07:16,804 --> 00:07:20,142
Wow, you look amazing!

105
00:07:21,695 --> 00:07:22,999
What?

106
00:07:22,999 --> 00:07:24,792
Why?

107
00:07:34,375 --> 00:07:36,613
We're not that close, are we?

108
00:07:37,855 --> 00:07:40,809
Don't touch me.

109
00:07:46,549 --> 00:07:48,781
I'll get going.

110
00:07:48,781 --> 00:07:50,481
Yeah, sure.

111
00:08:12,815 --> 00:08:16,032
Shall we go now?

112
00:08:17,341 --> 00:08:18,747
Yeah.

113
00:08:32,688 --> 00:08:34,388
Woo Jae said no.

114
00:08:35,048 --> 00:08:37,315
How could he just show up right then?

115
00:08:37,315 --> 00:08:39,192
What great timing.

116
00:08:39,855 --> 00:08:43,039
And why would you grab his waist at that time?

117
00:08:43,801 --> 00:08:44,939
Anyway!

118
00:08:44,939 --> 00:08:47,607
Let's rethink who the first guest should be.

119
00:08:49,068 --> 00:08:50,875
Who could we get?

120
00:08:51,489 --> 00:08:54,128
Have you got anyone in mind?

121
00:08:54,128 --> 00:08:56,272
<i>What is she talking about right now?</i>

122
00:08:56,272 --> 00:08:57,796
<i>Say something!</i>

123
00:08:57,796 --> 00:09:00,399
<i>I'm thinking, just keep quiet, will you?</i>

124
00:09:00,399 --> 00:09:02,088
<i>Why are you giving me that look?
What do you want?</i>

125
00:09:02,088 --> 00:09:05,035
<i>Keep your mouth shut and your eyes down
if you want to live.</i>

126
00:09:05,035 --> 00:09:06,735
What are you guys doing?

127
00:09:07,435 --> 00:09:08,959
What's this?

128
00:09:08,959 --> 00:09:11,321
Is it some kind of meme?

129
00:09:11,321 --> 00:09:12,672
Oh, wait...

130
00:09:12,672 --> 00:09:15,929
- Did you just curse at me or something?
- No, it's just...

131
00:09:17,615 --> 00:09:18,735
[One Meal with Ha Ru: One and Only Table]

132
00:09:20,588 --> 00:09:22,703
<i>You're so popular right now,</i>

133
00:09:22,703 --> 00:09:25,676
<i>advertisers are dying to get product placement
on "One Meal with Ha Ru."</i>

134
00:09:25,676 --> 00:09:31,341
<i>That's why we're launching the spin-off,
"One and Only Table," right away.</i>

135
00:09:35,055 --> 00:09:36,755
<i>So this is it.</i>

136
00:09:39,500 --> 00:09:41,371
What should I do?

137
00:09:45,468 --> 00:09:49,391
Jung Woo Jae says he'd rather die,
and we don't have much time left until we film.

138
00:09:51,115 --> 00:09:56,295
First things first, we'll have to film
without a guest for the pilot.

139
00:09:56,295 --> 00:09:57,945
But...

140
00:09:57,945 --> 00:10:00,951
Why won't Woo Jae do it?

141
00:10:09,928 --> 00:10:11,827
The reality show...

142
00:10:11,827 --> 00:10:13,681
It looked like it'd be fun.

143
00:10:13,681 --> 00:10:15,245
If you took the offer,

144
00:10:15,245 --> 00:10:16,909
I'd get to visit Haesol in such a long time.

145
00:10:16,909 --> 00:10:19,148
Seems nice.

146
00:10:19,148 --> 00:10:22,225
We could get Ha Ru's father
to cook us up something nice.

147
00:10:23,008 --> 00:10:24,572
His mother's raw fish in cold broth
is a killer, too.

148
00:10:24,572 --> 00:10:28,448
You'd take one sip of that iced broth...

149
00:10:28,448 --> 00:10:30,132
so cold it gives you a brain freeze,

150
00:10:30,132 --> 00:10:32,941
and the hotness of the sauce
comes hitting you right back...

151
00:10:32,941 --> 00:10:36,008
Hot and sour, you remember, right?
Yoon's raw fish in cold broth!

152
00:10:36,008 --> 00:10:38,741
- Keep your eyes on the road.
- Oh, sorry.

153
00:10:41,335 --> 00:10:43,035
<i>You're still...</i>

154
00:10:44,775 --> 00:10:46,808
<i>not over it, are you?</i>

155
00:10:48,949 --> 00:10:50,053
<i>Woo Jae.</i>

156
00:10:50,053 --> 00:10:53,117
<i>The breakup was ten years ago, not one.</i>

157
00:10:53,117 --> 00:10:55,387
<i>You're not 24 anymore, you're 34.</i>

158
00:10:55,387 --> 00:10:58,316
<i>I won't force you
to do anything you don't want.</i>

159
00:10:58,975 --> 00:11:01,141
<i>But after ten whole years...</i>

160
00:11:01,141 --> 00:11:04,462
<i>Shouldn't it have gotten better
than what it's like right now?</i>

161
00:11:04,462 --> 00:11:06,162
<i>Your heart, I mean.</i>

162
00:11:08,295 --> 00:11:10,328
<i>Whether you're still in love,</i>

163
00:11:11,135 --> 00:11:13,887
<i>or just stubborn and scabbed over...</i>

164
00:11:15,702 --> 00:11:18,051
<i>you should come to terms with it now.</i>

165
00:11:18,636 --> 00:11:20,925
<i>Do it for the sake of your own heart,
Jung Woo Jae.</i>

166
00:11:42,932 --> 00:11:44,645
Where are we going, anyway?

167
00:11:44,645 --> 00:11:47,729
My schedule is over. Aren't we going home?

168
00:11:47,729 --> 00:11:50,354
You have dinner with Gyeong Woo.

169
00:11:51,732 --> 00:11:53,192
- I'm good.
- "I'm good."

170
00:11:53,192 --> 00:11:54,365
"You two go on ahead."

171
00:11:54,365 --> 00:11:57,116
That won't fly anymore,
you've already said that the last three times.

172
00:11:57,116 --> 00:11:59,593
Besides, Pyo Gyeong Woo
wants this dinner so bad

173
00:11:59,593 --> 00:12:02,977
that he's spent the last hour
drinking coffee near the restaurant.

174
00:12:09,325 --> 00:12:10,999
But...

175
00:12:10,999 --> 00:12:13,947
Why won't Woo Jae do it?

176
00:12:15,819 --> 00:12:18,470
What do you mean, why?

177
00:12:21,979 --> 00:12:24,979
Oh, no, it's nothing! Nothing to worry about.

178
00:12:24,979 --> 00:12:26,959
What is it?

179
00:12:26,959 --> 00:12:28,722
What's his reason?

180
00:12:30,092 --> 00:12:32,045
- Yoon Ha Ru.
- Yeah?

181
00:12:32,045 --> 00:12:33,663
Huh?

182
00:12:33,663 --> 00:12:37,092
No, not you, Ha Na. Ha Ru. Yoon Ha Ru.

183
00:12:37,092 --> 00:12:38,429
Oh, right.

184
00:12:38,429 --> 00:12:40,100
Yeah.

185
00:12:40,100 --> 00:12:41,530
What is it?

186
00:12:42,179 --> 00:12:43,803
<i>Why is she staring like that?</i>

187
00:12:43,803 --> 00:12:46,274
<i>Did she... catch on to something?</i>

188
00:12:47,865 --> 00:12:49,565
Babe.

189
00:12:50,279 --> 00:12:53,565
Could you just shut up for ten seconds, please?

190
00:12:53,565 --> 00:12:56,362
Oh, who's a good boy?

191
00:12:58,299 --> 00:13:02,377
I'm not even married yet,
but it seems like I've already got a son.

192
00:13:05,469 --> 00:13:08,046
Well, Ha Na.

193
00:13:10,302 --> 00:13:12,026
You and Woo Jae...

194
00:13:12,026 --> 00:13:14,998
It may have been ten years
since you guys broke up,

195
00:13:14,998 --> 00:13:17,261
but I still think you need
to be more thoughtful.

196
00:13:17,261 --> 00:13:20,415
And speaking of thoughtfulness
between ex-lovers,

197
00:13:20,415 --> 00:13:24,179
I think it'd be fairer for the one
who got over faster to be the more mindful one.

198
00:13:24,179 --> 00:13:25,903
For example, what you just did back there,

199
00:13:25,903 --> 00:13:29,267
- touching him, would make him feel...
<i>- Does she mean Woo Jae and I broke up?</i>

200
00:13:29,267 --> 00:13:31,728
<i>And I'm the one who caused it?</i>

201
00:13:34,715 --> 00:13:36,439
Just a moment.

202
00:13:36,439 --> 00:13:37,885
Hello?

203
00:13:42,725 --> 00:13:45,419
- I told you that schedule is not going to work!
- You need to go, now.

204
00:13:45,419 --> 00:13:47,215
- Me?
- Woo Jae's new movie

205
00:13:47,215 --> 00:13:49,203
- starts shooting next month, and...
- I don't know.

206
00:13:49,203 --> 00:13:52,709
the overseas promotion for
the last series, on top of that,

207
00:13:52,709 --> 00:13:55,710
we need three days just for moving!

208
00:13:56,802 --> 00:13:58,386
- What do I do?
- We need to go together.

209
00:13:58,386 --> 00:14:01,150
- Take me with you.
- Do you really think that?

210
00:14:01,150 --> 00:14:05,035
If you offer a higher fee,
we'll operate everything?

211
00:14:05,035 --> 00:14:07,319
No, that's not how it works.

212
00:14:07,319 --> 00:14:08,751
- Hey, you know what?
- Excuse me.

213
00:14:08,751 --> 00:14:12,755
- Instead of trying to convince me on the phone,
- Wait, wait!

214
00:14:12,755 --> 00:14:13,946
What do I do?

215
00:14:13,946 --> 00:14:17,447
why don't you go back
and work out the schedule again?

216
00:14:39,102 --> 00:14:42,662
[Lost Time]

217
00:14:43,609 --> 00:14:45,333
Let's start now.

218
00:14:45,333 --> 00:14:47,633
Ready... Action!

219
00:14:48,689 --> 00:14:52,009
So you want me to take stuff out of the bag

220
00:14:52,009 --> 00:14:55,009
and show it to you, is that right?

221
00:14:55,009 --> 00:14:57,135
Okay. Kind of pointless, but sure.

222
00:14:58,315 --> 00:15:00,762
Hello. Say hello!

223
00:15:00,762 --> 00:15:01,818
Oh, okay.

224
00:15:01,818 --> 00:15:02,828
[Hi to the camera]

225
00:15:02,828 --> 00:15:05,159
Yeah, hi, hi.

226
00:15:05,159 --> 00:15:07,043
Hello, or whatever.

227
00:15:08,895 --> 00:15:11,644
I'll do... whatever this is, today!

228
00:15:21,662 --> 00:15:23,322
It's a hat.

229
00:15:23,322 --> 00:15:26,219
Probably for days
when I haven't washed my hair.

230
00:15:26,219 --> 00:15:28,895
To protect others' eyes and noses...

231
00:15:28,895 --> 00:15:32,344
from my odor, you see.

232
00:15:32,989 --> 00:15:34,429
In fact, Yoon Ha Na...

233
00:15:34,429 --> 00:15:36,413
No, no. I mean, I...

234
00:15:36,413 --> 00:15:41,039
I don't wash my hair very much on my days off.

235
00:15:43,769 --> 00:15:44,895
Let's see...

236
00:15:46,195 --> 00:15:47,893
Sunglasses. I see.

237
00:15:47,893 --> 00:15:51,683
Ah! I know. These are for
hiding my face without makeup.

238
00:15:51,683 --> 00:15:54,005
Or... Maybe not.

239
00:15:54,005 --> 00:15:56,392
Maybe it's for glaring at people.

240
00:15:58,209 --> 00:16:01,293
Guys, can you see my eyes right now?

241
00:16:01,293 --> 00:16:03,150
You can't, right?

242
00:16:03,150 --> 00:16:06,094
There's always something
that pisses you off at work.

243
00:16:06,094 --> 00:16:08,345
That's where these come in.

244
00:16:08,345 --> 00:16:09,931
To glare at people.

245
00:16:11,295 --> 00:16:14,429
Now, let's see what we've got here.

246
00:16:14,429 --> 00:16:17,039
Here we have a keychain.

247
00:16:17,039 --> 00:16:18,739
It's...

248
00:16:24,189 --> 00:16:25,829
Now...

249
00:16:25,829 --> 00:16:31,053
You can, of course, just eat
this tender charcoal-grilled beef as is,

250
00:16:31,053 --> 00:16:34,603
but if you drink this 80-year-old-recipe
Pyongyang cold noodle broth with it,

251
00:16:34,603 --> 00:16:36,964
it's good enough to kill! See?

252
00:16:40,709 --> 00:16:44,284
[One Meal with Ha Ru: One and Only Table]
<i>Big announcement incoming!</i>

253
00:16:44,284 --> 00:16:46,709
<i>- The popular cooking show</i>
- The trailer is out already.

254
00:16:46,709 --> 00:16:48,244
<i>that took the nation by hunger,</i>

255
00:16:48,244 --> 00:16:49,937
<i>"One and Only Table!"</i>

256
00:16:49,937 --> 00:16:51,394
<i>- Coming soon!</i>
- What's the deal with Ha Na?

257
00:16:51,394 --> 00:16:54,292
She just doesn't seem to grow old.

258
00:16:55,798 --> 00:16:58,382
What do you think her secret is?

259
00:16:58,382 --> 00:17:00,439
- Hey, have some of this meat, too.
- It's amazing how good she looks.

260
00:17:00,439 --> 00:17:01,897
You've just been drinking this whole time.

261
00:17:01,897 --> 00:17:04,120
- But I am eating.
- She hasn't changed a bit.

262
00:17:06,449 --> 00:17:08,579
Come to think of it, what's it been?

263
00:17:08,579 --> 00:17:10,150
Ten years?

264
00:17:10,150 --> 00:17:11,362
It's been ten years, right?

265
00:17:11,362 --> 00:17:12,922
Okay.

266
00:17:12,922 --> 00:17:14,573
I can say it with ease now.

267
00:17:14,573 --> 00:17:16,615
If I'm being honest, you...

268
00:17:17,389 --> 00:17:19,693
When I heard you and Ha Na
were dating, well, I...

269
00:17:19,693 --> 00:17:21,157
I was so jealous!

270
00:17:21,157 --> 00:17:23,054
Tell me, dating a goddess like that...

271
00:17:23,054 --> 00:17:25,069
What does it feel like?

272
00:17:25,069 --> 00:17:27,213
Does the world bloom with beauty?

273
00:17:27,213 --> 00:17:29,854
I doubt you ever got mad
when you were together.

274
00:17:33,209 --> 00:17:36,053
Anyway, why did you two even break up?

275
00:17:36,053 --> 00:17:38,537
You were perfect together!
Good-looking guy meets good-looking girl,

276
00:17:38,537 --> 00:17:41,551
- gets married...
- Hey, have this 80-year-old-recipe dumpling!

277
00:17:43,854 --> 00:17:46,362
Have some more beef.

278
00:17:50,035 --> 00:17:53,336
It was like they were in a movie
since their first day together.

279
00:17:53,942 --> 00:17:58,462
There are only a few moments in my life
that I just can't forget,

280
00:17:58,462 --> 00:18:00,162
and that day is one of them.

281
00:18:00,782 --> 00:18:03,189
Why? What was it like?

282
00:18:03,189 --> 00:18:04,833
Don't you remember, babe?

283
00:18:04,833 --> 00:18:06,919
We saw it together.

284
00:18:10,035 --> 00:18:12,527
I must be getting old.

285
00:18:13,422 --> 00:18:15,895
I forgot what happened.

286
00:18:15,895 --> 00:18:19,754
It was back in our university years,
when they were filming that short film.

287
00:18:20,462 --> 00:18:23,721
- Yeah?
- They had a really intense fight!

288
00:18:27,395 --> 00:18:28,846
<i>But what about me?</i>

289
00:18:28,846 --> 00:18:30,609
<i>How do you think that makes me feel?</i>

290
00:18:30,609 --> 00:18:33,246
<i>Like I'm helpless.
Like all I do is cause trouble.</i>

291
00:18:33,246 --> 00:18:34,989
<i>That's...</i>

292
00:18:34,989 --> 00:18:37,095
<i>That's what you make me feel like.</i>

293
00:18:37,702 --> 00:18:39,395
<i>I'm asking you.</i>

294
00:18:39,395 --> 00:18:40,853
<i>Please.</i>

295
00:18:40,853 --> 00:18:43,130
<i>Just live for yourself.</i>

296
00:18:43,130 --> 00:18:45,721
They were throwing such harsh words
at each other,

297
00:18:45,721 --> 00:18:48,177
when Lee Hyeong Won showed up.

298
00:18:50,695 --> 00:18:55,293
Right as I thought I might get to witness
a dopamine-filled love triangle in real life...

299
00:18:55,293 --> 00:18:56,881
<i>Yoon Ha Na!</i>

300
00:19:43,116 --> 00:19:44,327
<i>Ha Na.</i>

301
00:19:44,327 --> 00:19:45,766
<i>Are you okay?</i>

302
00:19:49,356 --> 00:19:50,827
With just one hug from Woo Jae,

303
00:19:50,827 --> 00:19:53,209
the whole vibe changed.

304
00:19:54,203 --> 00:19:55,633
<i>Yeah.</i>

305
00:19:59,503 --> 00:20:01,592
<i>I'm sorry, Ha Na.</i>

306
00:20:02,243 --> 00:20:05,353
<i>- I didn't mean to get into a fight...
- I like you.</i>

307
00:20:09,776 --> 00:20:11,222
<i>I...</i>

308
00:20:12,199 --> 00:20:14,595
<i>I like you. Jung Woo Jae.</i>

309
00:20:42,999 --> 00:20:45,483
While they were dating,

310
00:20:45,483 --> 00:20:47,433
what were they like?

311
00:20:47,433 --> 00:20:49,133
Did they seem happy?

312
00:20:52,659 --> 00:20:54,650
It was like the whole world...

313
00:20:54,650 --> 00:20:57,258
was an island
with just the two of them living on it.

314
00:20:57,886 --> 00:21:00,819
Devoid of any outside noise.

315
00:21:00,819 --> 00:21:04,016
A darn pretty island, I'd say.

316
00:21:12,199 --> 00:21:14,949
- That sounds good! I'm starving.
- You must be hungry.

317
00:21:14,949 --> 00:21:17,173
- What do you want to eat?
- I want meat!

318
00:21:17,173 --> 00:21:18,206
- Meat?
- Yeah.

319
00:21:18,206 --> 00:21:19,600
Oh, wait.

320
00:21:36,773 --> 00:21:38,703
What are you hiding?

321
00:21:38,703 --> 00:21:40,369
Ta-da!

322
00:21:50,946 --> 00:21:52,468
It tickles!

323
00:21:53,379 --> 00:21:55,079
What are you doing?

324
00:21:58,686 --> 00:22:01,085
- This is awful!
- Hey, babe.

325
00:22:04,899 --> 00:22:07,013
Babe! Babe!

326
00:22:08,553 --> 00:22:10,024
What was that?

327
00:22:12,399 --> 00:22:13,861
What are you looking at?

328
00:22:23,159 --> 00:22:29,657
We're here today with Jung Woo Jae,
who stole every woman's heart

329
00:22:29,657 --> 00:22:31,916
with the 2017 drama, "The Boy from the Moon."

330
00:22:31,916 --> 00:22:34,503
This may be a touchy subject,

331
00:22:34,503 --> 00:22:38,985
but everyone is just dying to know,
so I can't help but ask.

332
00:22:38,985 --> 00:22:43,452
Do you, perhaps, have a girlfriend?

333
00:22:46,909 --> 00:22:49,385
Yes, I do.

334
00:22:49,385 --> 00:22:51,266
We definitely weren't expecting that.

335
00:22:51,266 --> 00:22:54,374
Are we the first to officially hear about this?

336
00:22:54,374 --> 00:22:58,201
Yeah, I'd say so. We're doing great.

337
00:22:58,854 --> 00:23:00,559
[The Masked Season]
Next up...

338
00:23:00,559 --> 00:23:06,385
We have with us the actress Yoon Ha Na,
nicknamed the Jeon Hee Ae of short films.

339
00:23:06,385 --> 00:23:08,722
We are taking questions now.

340
00:23:09,733 --> 00:23:15,638
This is your first appearance in a title role
in a drama with "The Masked Season."

341
00:23:15,638 --> 00:23:18,950
However, some have compared you with
the other actors, Jeon Hee Ae and Ha Dong Jin,

342
00:23:18,950 --> 00:23:22,587
voicing concerns about the difference
in your proficiency in acting.

343
00:23:22,587 --> 00:23:28,189
We want to know if you felt like
you were lacking skills yourself.

344
00:23:31,857 --> 00:23:33,975
Well, first of all,

345
00:23:33,975 --> 00:23:38,436
I was grateful to be able to work
side-by-side with such big names.

346
00:23:38,436 --> 00:23:40,595
It was a true honor.

347
00:23:41,365 --> 00:23:48,268
I tried my best not to get in the way
of my seniors and colleagues.

348
00:23:48,268 --> 00:23:51,599
I hope you'll take kindly to my efforts.

349
00:23:53,678 --> 00:23:57,143
You just mentioned
"a difference in proficiency," yes?

350
00:23:58,705 --> 00:24:04,644
Truthfully speaking, both Hee Ae and I were
in awe of how good Ha Na's acting was on set.

351
00:24:04,644 --> 00:24:07,597
Her ability to read intentions
beyond what is shown,

352
00:24:07,597 --> 00:24:12,364
and her almost explosive charisma
that takes over the whole set.

353
00:24:12,364 --> 00:24:14,270
If I may say so,

354
00:24:14,270 --> 00:24:20,253
I truly think that I was lucky to have had
actress Yoon Ha Na as my counterpart.

355
00:24:20,253 --> 00:24:23,126
Actress Yoon Ha Na is, promptly speaking,

356
00:24:23,126 --> 00:24:28,107
an actress of great proficiency
who helped me step beyond my own shortcomings.

357
00:24:32,133 --> 00:24:34,137
The expertise of an actor

358
00:24:34,137 --> 00:24:38,135
isn't determined by the length
of their career or resume.

359
00:24:38,135 --> 00:24:44,994
You'll have to see Yoon Ha Na's acting skills
for yourself when the program airs.

360
00:24:49,842 --> 00:24:51,992
Any more questions?

361
00:24:54,397 --> 00:24:55,735
Ms. Yoon Ha Na!

362
00:24:55,735 --> 00:25:00,375
Just now, actor Jung Woo Jae admitted
to a love scandal on a live interview.

363
00:25:00,375 --> 00:25:04,776
Everyone is pointing you out
as the missing piece.

364
00:25:04,776 --> 00:25:07,498
Is there any truth to this?

365
00:25:25,732 --> 00:25:30,169
This is my first time
hearing about this as well.

366
00:25:30,816 --> 00:25:33,093
Mr. Jung Woo Jae is...

367
00:25:37,486 --> 00:25:42,146
Just a longtime childhood friend of mine.

368
00:25:42,146 --> 00:25:45,223
He's a great actor, that's all I think of him.

369
00:25:45,223 --> 00:25:47,017
I ask you not to make any more assumptions,

370
00:25:47,017 --> 00:25:51,704
and to stay on the topic of our show,
"The Masked Season."

371
00:25:53,384 --> 00:25:55,763
Any other questions?

372
00:26:01,497 --> 00:26:03,605
What do you want to do?

373
00:26:03,605 --> 00:26:07,865
I'll clean up after you,
but the decision is yours.

374
00:26:14,912 --> 00:26:16,856
I'm sorry.

375
00:26:16,856 --> 00:26:18,796
I wasn't thinking straight.

376
00:26:18,796 --> 00:26:21,218
I should've asked you first.

377
00:26:21,830 --> 00:26:23,922
No, I'm sorry.

378
00:26:23,922 --> 00:26:25,705
I was just so...

379
00:26:25,705 --> 00:26:28,751
caught off guard, and it scared me.

380
00:26:28,751 --> 00:26:30,900
I didn't mean to lie.

381
00:26:32,682 --> 00:26:34,964
You guys are so dramatic.

382
00:26:43,124 --> 00:26:46,242
If we admit it now and change our statement,

383
00:26:46,242 --> 00:26:49,013
it would make Ha Na a liar.

384
00:26:50,750 --> 00:26:55,581
I want to keep who I'm dating a secret.

385
00:26:55,581 --> 00:26:57,705
You'd do that for us, right?

386
00:26:59,835 --> 00:27:01,269
Sure.

387
00:27:02,586 --> 00:27:05,417
I'm so sorry, Woo Jae.

388
00:27:05,417 --> 00:27:07,693
No, I'm the one who should be sorry.

389
00:27:07,693 --> 00:27:10,339
You just focus on your show, okay?

390
00:27:11,991 --> 00:27:14,188
Why are you crying?

391
00:27:14,188 --> 00:27:16,213
- Hey, don't cry.
- I'm really sorry.

392
00:27:16,213 --> 00:27:18,186
No, I'm sorry.

393
00:27:19,730 --> 00:27:21,430
Hey, don't cry.

394
00:27:22,125 --> 00:27:24,765
They were inseparable like that, but...

395
00:27:51,833 --> 00:27:53,857
Did Yoon Ha Na...

396
00:27:53,857 --> 00:27:56,917
do something really bad or something?

397
00:27:59,813 --> 00:28:04,986
I've just been having some trouble
remembering things these days.

398
00:28:04,986 --> 00:28:09,203
Well, she must've had her reasons.

399
00:28:09,203 --> 00:28:13,767
But for Woo Jae, it must've felt like
she denied his whole existence.

400
00:28:13,767 --> 00:28:17,093
He went away to serve in the army
at the peak of his popularity,

401
00:28:17,093 --> 00:28:20,593
and I couldn't even stop him.
He seemed so miserable.

402
00:28:20,593 --> 00:28:22,130
Denied?

403
00:28:22,130 --> 00:28:24,517
It's whatever.
Let's stop talking about those two.

404
00:28:24,517 --> 00:28:27,466
- W-wait, I...
- Anyway, babe?

405
00:28:27,466 --> 00:28:30,270
- Yeah?
- We...

406
00:28:30,270 --> 00:28:32,880
have some catching up to do, don't you think?

407
00:28:35,966 --> 00:28:37,279
What do you mean?

408
00:28:37,279 --> 00:28:39,186
What do you think?

409
00:28:39,186 --> 00:28:41,897
Let's move on from others' love lives...

410
00:28:43,519 --> 00:28:45,874
and into ours now.

411
00:28:49,463 --> 00:28:51,481
Babe.

412
00:28:51,481 --> 00:28:53,640
You're not going home tonight.

413
00:29:02,736 --> 00:29:04,213
Hey!

414
00:29:04,853 --> 00:29:06,526
I...

415
00:29:07,137 --> 00:29:09,186
It's...

416
00:29:10,377 --> 00:29:12,883
- What?
- I mean...

417
00:29:12,883 --> 00:29:14,550
I just...

418
00:29:14,550 --> 00:29:16,001
I'm saying...

419
00:29:16,001 --> 00:29:19,796
<i>This can't be happening.
How do I get out of this?</i>

420
00:29:20,737 --> 00:29:22,356
I love you.

421
00:29:23,717 --> 00:29:26,657
I really love you, Seo Ye Rang...

422
00:29:26,657 --> 00:29:28,590
But I...

423
00:29:28,590 --> 00:29:30,369
I'm like...

424
00:29:32,403 --> 00:29:34,214
Really...

425
00:29:34,214 --> 00:29:37,005
- I'm not feeling good today.
- Huh?

426
00:29:37,005 --> 00:29:39,717
You're sick? Why? How?

427
00:29:39,717 --> 00:29:42,747
Well, I'm feeling...

428
00:29:42,747 --> 00:29:45,924
Tell me! Where does it hurt?

429
00:29:47,157 --> 00:29:49,339
Actually, I'm...

430
00:29:51,070 --> 00:29:52,541
Never mind.

431
00:29:52,541 --> 00:29:55,639
If I tell you, I'll just make you sad.

432
00:29:57,910 --> 00:30:01,554
I'll tell you tomorrow.

433
00:30:01,554 --> 00:30:03,217
- Tomorrow.
- Tomorrow?

434
00:30:03,217 --> 00:30:07,183
Yes! I'll just get going now.

435
00:30:08,103 --> 00:30:09,850
I'll call you!

436
00:30:09,850 --> 00:30:11,741
Y-you're leaving like this?

437
00:30:12,543 --> 00:30:15,813
<i>I'm sorry, Yoon Ha Ru. Sorry, Ye Rang!</i>

438
00:30:18,563 --> 00:30:20,263
Hey!

439
00:30:21,283 --> 00:30:23,510
That bastard!

440
00:30:23,510 --> 00:30:25,848
He better not be cheating!

441
00:30:33,417 --> 00:30:36,881
If you check the seat pocket,
there's a script for you.

442
00:30:36,881 --> 00:30:38,581
Oh, this?

443
00:30:40,299 --> 00:30:41,675
[Lost Time, Written by Chu Si Hwan]
"Lost Time?"

444
00:30:41,675 --> 00:30:43,468
It's a new script.

445
00:30:43,468 --> 00:30:45,821
The director only wanted you to have it.

446
00:30:45,821 --> 00:30:47,399
- Is that so?
- Yeah.

447
00:30:47,399 --> 00:30:49,956
It's a rookie director, I heard. Take a look.

448
00:30:49,956 --> 00:30:54,447
The development team said it's the best one
they've had come in the whole year!

449
00:30:54,447 --> 00:30:56,824
- Sure, I'll check it out.
- Yes, ma'am!

450
00:30:56,824 --> 00:30:59,161
And before you shoot
the reality show in two days,

451
00:30:59,161 --> 00:31:01,788
the CEO arranged a meeting with the director.

452
00:31:01,788 --> 00:31:03,239
Okay, okay.

453
00:31:03,239 --> 00:31:07,828
Our Boss really likes to keep a tight schedule.

454
00:31:40,668 --> 00:31:42,841
<i>Woo Jae, just let it go already.</i>

455
00:31:42,841 --> 00:31:46,645
<i>I'll get you something nicer, please?</i>

456
00:31:46,645 --> 00:31:49,062
<i>Good job today. You can go home now.</i>

457
00:31:49,062 --> 00:31:51,346
<i>Seriously, this isn't an antique shop!</i>

458
00:31:51,346 --> 00:31:53,747
<i>There's plenty of ready-made stuff
that gets the job done!</i>

459
00:31:53,747 --> 00:31:55,582
<i>Go away.</i>

460
00:31:55,582 --> 00:31:56,686
<i>Okay.</i>

461
00:31:58,515 --> 00:32:00,068
<i>What's wrong?</i>

462
00:32:00,068 --> 00:32:02,881
<i>Give it over here, I'll do it for you.</i>

463
00:32:02,881 --> 00:32:05,005
<i>- What are you doing?
- No way.</i>

464
00:32:05,005 --> 00:32:08,715
<i>It only has meaning
if I made every last bit myself.</i>

465
00:32:08,715 --> 00:32:11,412
<i>Do whatever you want. I'm going.</i>

466
00:32:11,412 --> 00:32:13,004
<i>Just go easy on it and go to bed on time.</i>

467
00:32:13,004 --> 00:32:15,450
<i>Thanks for putting up with me.</i>

468
00:32:47,248 --> 00:32:48,948
<i>They're perfect.</i>

469
00:33:02,274 --> 00:33:03,708
<i>- This way.
- Huh?</i>

470
00:33:03,708 --> 00:33:05,707
<i>- What is it?
- Come on.</i>

471
00:33:21,081 --> 00:33:22,525
<i>What's this?</i>

472
00:33:22,525 --> 00:33:23,872
<i>Open it.</i>

473
00:33:24,527 --> 00:33:26,227
<i>What could it be?</i>

474
00:33:37,181 --> 00:33:38,595
<i>What do you think?</i>

475
00:33:40,635 --> 00:33:43,423
<i>Did you make this yourself?</i>

476
00:33:43,423 --> 00:33:44,895
<i>Yes. I...</i>

477
00:33:44,895 --> 00:33:47,819
<i>I wanted to make the pinnacle
of the analog and vintage aesthetic.</i>

478
00:33:47,819 --> 00:33:50,070
<i>There's just one in this world.</i>

479
00:33:51,581 --> 00:33:55,058
<i>Analog and vintage aesthetic.</i>

480
00:34:01,155 --> 00:34:02,592
<i>Hi.</i>

481
00:34:07,631 --> 00:34:09,331
<i>Hey, Jung Woo Jae.</i>

482
00:34:12,385 --> 00:34:14,358
<i>This is unbelievable.</i>

483
00:34:16,871 --> 00:34:18,345
<i>Ha Na?</i>

484
00:34:18,345 --> 00:34:19,670
<i>What's the matter?</i>

485
00:34:20,358 --> 00:34:22,466
<i>I just can't with you anymore.</i>

486
00:34:25,358 --> 00:34:29,719
<i>I guess you don't like the vintage aesthetic...</i>

487
00:34:36,098 --> 00:34:37,702
<i>I can't with you...</i>

488
00:34:37,702 --> 00:34:40,330
<i>being so cute!</i>

489
00:34:40,330 --> 00:34:42,431
<i>I'm... cute?</i>

490
00:34:42,431 --> 00:34:45,210
<i>So cute that I can't hold it in anymore.</i>

491
00:34:45,911 --> 00:34:49,933
<i>This keychain is so, so cute, too!</i>

492
00:34:51,865 --> 00:34:54,802
<i>I'll cherish it forever, until I die!</i>

493
00:34:54,802 --> 00:34:56,773
<i>In fact, when the Grim Reaper comes for me,</i>

494
00:34:56,773 --> 00:34:59,311
<i>I'll ask him to let me take it with me.</i>

495
00:34:59,311 --> 00:35:02,487
<i>The Grim Reaper? Now that's a stretch.</i>

496
00:35:11,724 --> 00:35:13,421
<i>Thank you.</i>

497
00:35:13,421 --> 00:35:14,881
<i>Thank you, too.</i>

498
00:35:14,881 --> 00:35:16,288
<i>I love it so much.</i>

499
00:35:16,288 --> 00:35:17,988
<i>- Really?
- Yeah.</i>

500
00:36:43,741 --> 00:36:46,575
What do I do now?

501
00:37:14,135 --> 00:37:15,835
[Yoon Ha Na, 2013 Best New Actress,
2022 Best Supporting Actress]

502
00:37:16,448 --> 00:37:17,986
That's all?

503
00:37:17,986 --> 00:37:20,105
Where's her Best Actress Award?

504
00:37:25,788 --> 00:37:28,521
"Failed to secure a leading role?"

505
00:37:28,521 --> 00:37:30,832
"Made her career
as a high-end supporting actress?"

506
00:37:30,832 --> 00:37:32,347
Woah.

507
00:37:34,255 --> 00:37:36,061
[Baekryong Film Awards terrorism]

508
00:37:38,028 --> 00:37:40,288
[Actor Hyun Seong Jae, Fashion Terrorist?]
[Terror on the Red Carpet, the Actress who Fell]

509
00:37:43,068 --> 00:37:45,888
So this is how it changed this time.

510
00:37:45,888 --> 00:37:47,601
Wait a minute.

511
00:37:47,601 --> 00:37:49,059
Then...

512
00:37:50,588 --> 00:37:51,961
[Lee Hyeong Won]

513
00:37:53,261 --> 00:37:54,939
[Lee Hyeong Won, 2026 Arcadia Gold Medalist]

514
00:37:54,939 --> 00:37:59,472
Darn it, so he took my gold medal!

515
00:38:02,988 --> 00:38:04,748
["Judo Hero" Lee Hyeong Won Disappears: Why?]
Disappeared?

516
00:38:07,615 --> 00:38:08,760
[Account Unavailable]

517
00:38:10,621 --> 00:38:12,847
It's got to be this bastard.

518
00:38:12,847 --> 00:38:14,547
Lee Hyeong Won...

519
00:38:17,621 --> 00:38:19,439
- There you are.
- Where's the camcorder?

520
00:38:19,439 --> 00:38:20,509
- In your room.
- Okay.

521
00:38:20,509 --> 00:38:22,209
No, not there!

522
00:38:23,821 --> 00:38:25,344
That one.

523
00:38:51,281 --> 00:38:55,535
Well... it does seem that
the situation has changed a little.

524
00:39:06,075 --> 00:39:09,022
What could I have possibly done to Woo Jae?

525
00:39:13,988 --> 00:39:15,472
Hey.

526
00:39:18,335 --> 00:39:19,752
What?

527
00:39:19,752 --> 00:39:21,452
Are you okay?

528
00:39:23,268 --> 00:39:25,392
Why wouldn't I be?

529
00:39:25,392 --> 00:39:27,263
Woo Jae is well and alive.

530
00:39:27,263 --> 00:39:28,994
You seem successful.

531
00:39:28,994 --> 00:39:30,547
And me...

532
00:39:31,608 --> 00:39:33,059
Well.

533
00:39:33,059 --> 00:39:37,129
I'm still acting, at least.

534
00:39:39,681 --> 00:39:41,085
What now?

535
00:39:41,085 --> 00:39:43,896
What's with that face?
It's not like you to look so melancholic.

536
00:39:43,896 --> 00:39:47,035
I mean, your career as an actress aside,

537
00:39:47,035 --> 00:39:51,132
it kind of feels like
I took your house away, you know.

538
00:39:51,132 --> 00:39:53,776
"Took it away?" You've got to be kidding me.

539
00:39:53,776 --> 00:39:57,479
At least you're letting me live with you.

540
00:39:59,875 --> 00:40:01,275
Hey, I'm your big brother.

541
00:40:01,275 --> 00:40:04,195
Just say the word,
and I'll buy you any house you want.

542
00:40:07,968 --> 00:40:10,391
About you quitting judo...

543
00:40:11,568 --> 00:40:13,833
I really was sorry.

544
00:40:18,035 --> 00:40:19,739
I guess winners win, though.

545
00:40:19,739 --> 00:40:23,400
You sure are something, Yoon Ha Ru.
You've made it as a chef, too.

546
00:40:23,995 --> 00:40:25,695
You've grown well.

547
00:40:29,488 --> 00:40:32,854
I sorted some things out while waiting for you.

548
00:40:34,515 --> 00:40:37,948
I never thought I'd see the day
Yoon Ha Ru grew up.

549
00:40:38,929 --> 00:40:40,628
First of all, how we returned to the present...

550
00:40:40,628 --> 00:40:42,475
[Remove battery: present, next leap: 2017]
is clear now.

551
00:40:42,475 --> 00:40:43,841
The removal of the battery.

552
00:40:43,841 --> 00:40:45,865
<i>Where do you think you're touching,
you bastard?</i>

553
00:40:45,865 --> 00:40:48,228
<i>Woah, what the heck!</i>

554
00:40:51,828 --> 00:40:53,668
If we travel to the past again,

555
00:40:53,668 --> 00:40:55,719
it'll probably be to the year 2017.

556
00:40:55,719 --> 00:40:57,809
Yeah. The only video left

557
00:40:57,809 --> 00:41:00,078
[2017 is the only thumbnail left]
is from 2017.

558
00:41:02,141 --> 00:41:04,399
The Best Actress Award...

559
00:41:04,399 --> 00:41:06,989
went to some other actress.

560
00:41:06,989 --> 00:41:10,273
The movie that you got the award for
was gone in the first place.

561
00:41:13,135 --> 00:41:14,419
It's fine.

562
00:41:14,419 --> 00:41:16,663
As long as Woo Jae is safe.

563
00:41:16,663 --> 00:41:18,347
And...

564
00:41:18,347 --> 00:41:20,047
This bastard.

565
00:41:20,689 --> 00:41:22,939
[Lee Hyeong Won]
"Arcadia Gold Medalist?"

566
00:41:22,939 --> 00:41:24,743
He retired after winning that gold medal.

567
00:41:24,743 --> 00:41:26,443
Dropped off the face of the earth.

568
00:41:28,015 --> 00:41:29,475
Disappeared?

569
00:41:29,475 --> 00:41:31,719
[We're back in the actual present time now]
<i>Yeah, it was all Lee Hyeong Won, that bastard.</i>

570
00:41:31,719 --> 00:41:34,073
<i>The stalking, Woo Jae's death... all of it.</i>

571
00:41:34,073 --> 00:41:36,430
<i>Something was going on even back then.</i>

572
00:41:39,235 --> 00:41:40,579
<i>But something's off.</i>

573
00:41:40,579 --> 00:41:43,528
<i>Hyeong Won wasn't there to hurt me that day.</i>

574
00:41:43,528 --> 00:41:45,165
<i>What?</i>

575
00:41:45,165 --> 00:41:46,709
Explain what you meant by that.

576
00:41:46,709 --> 00:41:51,050
If he wasn't there to hurt you,
why did he suddenly show up in Haesol?

577
00:41:53,161 --> 00:41:54,632
<i>Give it back.</i>

578
00:41:54,632 --> 00:41:57,105
<i>No, it's too dangerous.</i>

579
00:41:57,105 --> 00:41:58,663
<i>What?</i>

580
00:41:59,296 --> 00:42:01,527
<i>If you keep holding onto this, Yoon Ha Na...</i>

581
00:42:01,527 --> 00:42:03,227
<i>You'll be in danger.</i>

582
00:42:07,804 --> 00:42:09,015
Lee Hyeong Won...

583
00:42:09,015 --> 00:42:12,129
Apparently the coach and the chancellor
stopped him from taking part in the movie,

584
00:42:12,129 --> 00:42:16,096
which he worked so hard for, you know.

585
00:42:16,096 --> 00:42:19,691
He lost the male lead role,
and it just wasn't fair to him.

586
00:42:19,691 --> 00:42:22,176
He was really bummed out about it.

587
00:42:23,062 --> 00:42:25,402
He must have been feeling
conflicted about the whole thing,

588
00:42:25,402 --> 00:42:28,002
so he was just wandering around
near the practice room...

589
00:42:28,002 --> 00:42:32,967
That's when he saw someone suspicious.

590
00:42:32,967 --> 00:42:34,721
Suspicious?

591
00:42:38,025 --> 00:42:39,135
Yeah.

592
00:42:39,135 --> 00:42:41,453
He saw someone open my locker...

593
00:42:41,453 --> 00:42:44,137
and swap out my camcorder for a different one.

594
00:42:44,878 --> 00:42:47,318
Lee Hyeong Won happened to witness it.

595
00:43:11,558 --> 00:43:12,791
[Yoon Ha Na]

596
00:43:12,791 --> 00:43:14,491
<i>Yoon Ha Na's locker?</i>

597
00:43:15,651 --> 00:43:17,351
<i>That bastard!</i>

598
00:43:22,045 --> 00:43:23,564
<i>Hey, you.</i>

599
00:43:51,205 --> 00:43:52,905
[Yoon Ha Na]

600
00:43:54,541 --> 00:43:56,771
So he got the camcorder back.

601
00:43:56,771 --> 00:43:58,471
Did he see the bastard's face?

602
00:43:59,511 --> 00:44:01,517
No, he didn't.

603
00:44:01,517 --> 00:44:05,839
So, Lee Hyeong Won had the camcorder,
but didn't return it to you right away,

604
00:44:05,839 --> 00:44:09,883
and showed up at the filming set
to say it was because you'd be in danger?

605
00:44:09,883 --> 00:44:11,121
Do you seriously believe that?

606
00:44:11,121 --> 00:44:13,838
That Lee Hyeong Won
isn't the one after the camcorder?

607
00:44:13,838 --> 00:44:15,638
That's rich.

608
00:44:15,638 --> 00:44:18,675
Say we give him the benefit of the doubt,
and believe he wasn't after the camcorder.

609
00:44:18,675 --> 00:44:22,647
What does it even matter,
when Lee Hyeong Won killed Woo Jae?

610
00:44:23,365 --> 00:44:25,202
I guess.

611
00:44:25,202 --> 00:44:27,853
I was just so taken aback at the time.

612
00:44:27,853 --> 00:44:31,007
But you're right, he could've been lying.

613
00:44:31,731 --> 00:44:33,318
Lee Hyeong Won...

614
00:44:33,318 --> 00:44:36,658
We don't know
what he could be planning as we speak.

615
00:44:36,658 --> 00:44:40,253
The good news is that
Woo Jae is well and alive,

616
00:44:40,253 --> 00:44:42,884
and you weren't threatened
at the award ceremony.

617
00:44:43,538 --> 00:44:46,742
Sure, we're in each other's bodies,
and that is a problem.

618
00:44:46,742 --> 00:44:50,927
Worse than that,
the biggest variable posed to us is...

619
00:44:52,878 --> 00:44:54,578
- Lee Hyeong Won.
- Lee Hyeong Won.

620
00:45:08,991 --> 00:45:10,691
Damn it!

621
00:45:28,185 --> 00:45:31,044
- Good job, everyone.
- Good work, everyone.

622
00:45:32,210 --> 00:45:35,160
- Good work today.
- Good job.

623
00:45:35,160 --> 00:45:37,106
What are you doing on your day off tomorrow?

624
00:45:37,106 --> 00:45:39,178
Just resting. You should take a rest, too.

625
00:45:39,178 --> 00:45:40,885
This is your first break in a month.

626
00:45:40,885 --> 00:45:42,849
I heard Ha Ru is going to Haesol.

627
00:45:42,849 --> 00:45:46,177
He's going to do some research
and a pre-interview.

628
00:45:46,177 --> 00:45:48,285
I was thinking of going with him.

629
00:45:48,945 --> 00:45:53,051
I'm guessing you wouldn't want to go.

630
00:45:54,018 --> 00:45:55,245
Yeah.

631
00:45:55,245 --> 00:45:57,558
I changed my mind. I don't want to go!

632
00:45:57,558 --> 00:46:00,675
I didn't really want to go anyway.

633
00:46:00,675 --> 00:46:03,838
Right, you have a new script.

634
00:46:03,838 --> 00:46:05,095
Okay.

635
00:46:05,095 --> 00:46:06,311
Who's the director?

636
00:46:06,311 --> 00:46:09,462
It's a rookie, one I've never heard of before.

637
00:46:09,462 --> 00:46:11,353
The development team
is losing it over this one.

638
00:46:11,353 --> 00:46:14,692
They said it's even better than
Director Na Bong Chang's newest work.

639
00:46:15,400 --> 00:46:17,205
I'll give it a read.

640
00:46:17,205 --> 00:46:21,010
But from what I heard,
a copy went to Ha Na as well.

641
00:46:22,671 --> 00:46:24,175
The director...

642
00:46:24,175 --> 00:46:28,338
really wants you and Ha Na to film it together.

643
00:46:28,338 --> 00:46:29,769
That's what he wants.

644
00:46:35,125 --> 00:46:36,452
Is that so?

645
00:46:37,885 --> 00:46:39,585
Let's go, Woo Jae!

646
00:46:57,398 --> 00:47:00,558
[Lost Time]

647
00:47:10,765 --> 00:47:13,302
Wow, Seok Min, you're good at your job!

648
00:47:13,302 --> 00:47:15,652
- This coffee is amazing!
- Huh?

649
00:47:16,318 --> 00:47:19,725
It's just your favorite brand,
the one you always have.

650
00:47:19,725 --> 00:47:21,425
My favorite brand?

651
00:47:23,691 --> 00:47:26,384
Yoon Ha Na's taste buds
aren't that bad after all, huh?

652
00:47:27,085 --> 00:47:28,785
Whatever.

653
00:47:30,411 --> 00:47:33,634
Right, Ha Na. How did you like "Lost Time?"

654
00:47:34,271 --> 00:47:35,845
"Lost Time?"

655
00:47:35,845 --> 00:47:38,442
Yeah, the movie script I gave you last time.

656
00:47:38,442 --> 00:47:41,018
There's a meeting with the director today,
before the shoot.

657
00:47:41,018 --> 00:47:43,096
I told you last time.

658
00:47:45,558 --> 00:47:48,478
Oh, that!

659
00:47:48,478 --> 00:47:50,483
You didn't read it yet?

660
00:47:50,483 --> 00:47:53,863
Sorry, I'll read it now.

661
00:48:01,571 --> 00:48:04,245
[Lost Time, Written by Chu Si Hwan]

662
00:48:25,905 --> 00:48:27,333
Hey.

663
00:48:29,165 --> 00:48:31,152
What's that? It smells great.

664
00:48:31,152 --> 00:48:32,877
These.

665
00:48:33,465 --> 00:48:35,042
I like them.

666
00:48:35,042 --> 00:48:36,742
You need your coffee, right?

667
00:48:54,578 --> 00:48:58,002
Your coffee, sir.

668
00:48:58,002 --> 00:49:00,399
Here, the script for "Lost Time,"
the one I told you about.

669
00:49:00,399 --> 00:49:03,906
[Lost Time, Written by Chu Si Hwan]

670
00:49:22,991 --> 00:49:24,237
[Eun Soo, still mourning Yeong Hyeon,]

671
00:49:24,237 --> 00:49:26,697
[finds an old camcorder in the closet.]
"An old camcorder..."

672
00:49:43,351 --> 00:49:45,422
He must be out of his mind.

673
00:49:45,422 --> 00:49:46,994
This is...

674
00:49:46,994 --> 00:49:49,213
What is it? What's wrong?

675
00:49:49,213 --> 00:49:51,846
Well? Is it that good?

676
00:49:52,978 --> 00:49:54,678
It's not like that.

677
00:49:56,531 --> 00:49:58,038
[Lost Time]

678
00:49:58,038 --> 00:49:59,931
[Written by Chu Si Hwan]

679
00:50:19,891 --> 00:50:21,315
What is it?

680
00:50:23,851 --> 00:50:25,551
We found him.

681
00:50:32,371 --> 00:50:34,009
<i>You.</i>

682
00:50:34,009 --> 00:50:36,127
<i>Stop making me uncomfortable.</i>

683
00:50:37,471 --> 00:50:40,231
<i>What do you mean by that?</i>

684
00:50:40,231 --> 00:50:42,495
<i>Did I do something wrong?</i>

685
00:50:42,495 --> 00:50:45,579
<i>Saving me from danger.</i>

686
00:50:45,579 --> 00:50:48,511
<i>Making me feel guilty
over you getting hurt because of me.</i>

687
00:50:48,511 --> 00:50:51,729
<i>Giving me help that I never even asked for,
and making me feel sorry for it.</i>

688
00:50:51,729 --> 00:50:53,808
<i>I hate it.</i>

689
00:50:56,758 --> 00:51:02,371
"The two men, Yeong Hyeon and Jae Yoon,
don't hold back in their fight.

690
00:51:02,371 --> 00:51:04,051
Eun Soo cries out..."

691
00:51:04,051 --> 00:51:05,865
<i>- Stop it!</i>
- "Stop. Stop it..."

692
00:51:05,865 --> 00:51:07,565
<i>Please, stop.</i>

693
00:51:10,491 --> 00:51:13,578
"The camcorder in Jae Yoon's hand

694
00:51:13,578 --> 00:51:16,615
falls to the ground...

695
00:51:16,615 --> 00:51:20,063
As the battery falls out of the camcorder,

696
00:51:20,063 --> 00:51:21,664
fade-out."

697
00:51:23,305 --> 00:51:25,005
What is this?

698
00:51:29,285 --> 00:51:30,725
[Ye Rang]

699
00:51:33,271 --> 00:51:34,782
<i>Yes, Woo Jae?</i>

700
00:51:34,782 --> 00:51:37,918
It's me. I read the script.

701
00:51:37,918 --> 00:51:39,671
<i>The script? Which one?</i>

702
00:51:39,671 --> 00:51:41,269
<i>Anything catch your eye?</i>

703
00:51:41,269 --> 00:51:43,816
"Lost Time." Director Chu Si Hwan.

704
00:51:44,479 --> 00:51:47,269
Do you know the director, by any chance?

705
00:51:47,269 --> 00:51:50,146
<i>No, he's a rookie,
so I've never even met him yet.</i>

706
00:51:50,146 --> 00:51:51,670
<i>What's the matter?</i>

707
00:51:51,670 --> 00:51:55,211
Well... Have you read it yourself?

708
00:51:55,211 --> 00:52:00,968
Not yet. You do know that you get
a truckload of scripts, right?

709
00:52:01,931 --> 00:52:03,995
This... Chu Si Hwan.

710
00:52:03,995 --> 00:52:05,386
Is that his real name?

711
00:52:05,386 --> 00:52:07,777
<i>I don't know.</i>

712
00:52:07,777 --> 00:52:10,985
<i>We're meeting later today,
so I'll check and get back to you.</i>

713
00:52:10,985 --> 00:52:12,291
You're meeting today?

714
00:52:12,291 --> 00:52:13,311
<i>Yeah,</i>

715
00:52:13,311 --> 00:52:17,351
the development team was so pushy
about getting Ha Na to meet this guy.

716
00:52:17,351 --> 00:52:20,862
The director did say that
he wanted Ha Na as the female lead,

717
00:52:20,862 --> 00:52:24,313
<i>and it's a really good script,
so they wanted to seal the deal.</i>

718
00:52:24,313 --> 00:52:28,642
Besides, Ha Na has no reason
to decline a lead role at this point.

719
00:52:28,642 --> 00:52:30,713
When? Where?

720
00:52:31,982 --> 00:52:35,072
- Hey, Soo Hyuk. Let's go.
- Yes, sir!

721
00:52:46,969 --> 00:52:48,342
[Destination: Haesol Pine Trail]

722
00:53:00,169 --> 00:53:03,174
The person who knows
the secret of our camcorder,

723
00:53:03,174 --> 00:53:06,925
tried to hide it away...

724
00:53:06,925 --> 00:53:08,419
And...

725
00:53:09,489 --> 00:53:13,898
the one who deliberately dropped it
in front of my own eyes.

726
00:53:15,075 --> 00:53:16,871
It's all him.

727
00:53:17,582 --> 00:53:19,215
Chu Si Hwan?

728
00:53:22,042 --> 00:53:23,069
[Ye Rang]

729
00:53:26,102 --> 00:53:27,399
Yeah, Ye Rang?

730
00:53:27,399 --> 00:53:30,470
Ha Na, don't freak out and listen carefully.

731
00:53:30,470 --> 00:53:33,427
Woo Jae is on his way to Haesol.

732
00:53:33,427 --> 00:53:36,293
<i>He's going to be on "One and Only Table!"</i>

733
00:53:36,293 --> 00:53:38,253
Really? That's great.

734
00:53:38,253 --> 00:53:40,377
<i>I'll arrive there soon,</i>

735
00:53:40,377 --> 00:53:42,001
but I just have one thing to say,
as the trusted adult here.

736
00:53:42,001 --> 00:53:45,140
Just be careful,
it must've been a hard decision for him.

737
00:53:45,140 --> 00:53:46,671
Don't you dare hug him.

738
00:53:46,671 --> 00:53:48,175
<i>Don't even touch him!</i>

739
00:53:48,175 --> 00:53:51,145
Yeah, babe, I mean, Ye Rang!

740
00:53:51,145 --> 00:53:53,993
Have you read the script for "Lost Time" yet?

741
00:53:53,993 --> 00:53:56,760
<i>Not yet. I had so many
other ones to go through.</i>

742
00:53:56,760 --> 00:53:58,891
<i>Why? Is it any good?</i>

743
00:53:58,891 --> 00:54:01,161
Have you met the director?

744
00:54:01,161 --> 00:54:03,853
Is it someone you know?

745
00:54:03,853 --> 00:54:07,827
Everyone wants to know about
Director Chu Si Hwan today, huh?

746
00:54:07,827 --> 00:54:10,997
- Huh?
- Woo Jae just asked me about him, too.

747
00:54:10,997 --> 00:54:13,000
But I don't know him at all.

748
00:54:13,000 --> 00:54:15,049
Is the script that good?

749
00:55:00,400 --> 00:55:02,373
[One and Only Table]

750
00:55:03,400 --> 00:55:04,517
Chef.

751
00:55:04,517 --> 00:55:06,561
We have everything ready, just as you asked.

752
00:55:06,561 --> 00:55:08,960
But the main dish and cutlery
that the prop team got

753
00:55:08,960 --> 00:55:11,731
are too reflective
when filmed from the top-down.

754
00:55:11,731 --> 00:55:15,352
So, can I swap them out with the matte ones?

755
00:55:18,807 --> 00:55:21,437
Yeah, sure, let's do that.

756
00:55:21,437 --> 00:55:22,861
Yes, chef.

757
00:55:24,880 --> 00:55:26,637
You little imbecile!

758
00:55:26,637 --> 00:55:29,208
Who taught you so well, huh?

759
00:55:29,208 --> 00:55:31,310
Did you just slap my butt?

760
00:55:34,680 --> 00:55:36,166
Ha Na.

761
00:55:36,900 --> 00:55:38,660
What are you doing?

762
00:55:38,660 --> 00:55:41,266
I'm just proud of him.

763
00:55:57,229 --> 00:55:59,520
It's time, why isn't he here?

764
00:56:14,140 --> 00:56:15,811
- There you are.
- Hello.

765
00:56:15,811 --> 00:56:17,347
- We'll do the interview first.
- Okay.

766
00:56:17,347 --> 00:56:19,047
Come this way.

767
00:56:21,287 --> 00:56:23,418
- Right this way.
- Oh, right.

768
00:56:36,271 --> 00:56:39,573
Woo Jae made a big decision today.
I'm so proud of him.

769
00:56:39,573 --> 00:56:41,505
Thank you, Jung Woo Jae.

770
00:56:42,260 --> 00:56:44,677
Thank you so much, Woo Jae.

771
00:56:44,677 --> 00:56:46,628
It's for Ha Ru's sake.

772
00:56:46,628 --> 00:56:48,552
I'd do whatever I can to help him out.

773
00:56:48,552 --> 00:56:51,086
Wow, Woo Jae, you're so loyal!

774
00:56:53,933 --> 00:56:55,633
Hey, Seok Min!

775
00:56:57,980 --> 00:57:01,437
- Yes, ma'am.
- Where is Director Chu Si Hwan now?

776
00:57:01,437 --> 00:57:02,900
One moment.

777
00:57:05,173 --> 00:57:09,304
Director Chu Si Hwan apparently
came to Haesol on business, too.

778
00:57:09,304 --> 00:57:10,893
That's why I set the meeting up for today.

779
00:57:10,893 --> 00:57:12,333
You've all heard, right?

780
00:57:12,333 --> 00:57:14,244
If you come up a little further...

781
00:57:14,244 --> 00:57:16,288
You see me, right?

782
00:57:16,288 --> 00:57:17,986
This way!

783
00:57:17,986 --> 00:57:19,267
Hello.

784
00:57:19,267 --> 00:57:20,758
Let's go inside.

785
00:57:23,500 --> 00:57:25,656
Director Chu is here.

786
00:57:47,676 --> 00:57:49,906
Director Chu Si Hwan...

787
00:57:49,906 --> 00:57:52,032
was you, Jun Mo?

788
00:57:53,020 --> 00:57:55,120
It's been a while. Everyone.

789
00:57:56,900 --> 00:57:58,296
Woo Jae, you too.

790
00:58:01,820 --> 00:58:03,317
And Ha Na.

791
00:58:06,447 --> 00:58:08,887
I missed you guys. A lot.

792
00:58:50,386 --> 00:58:51,830
<i>I...</i>

793
00:58:51,830 --> 00:58:54,616
<i>wish the characters in my movie
were actually alive.</i>

794
00:58:55,512 --> 00:58:56,792
<i>The camcorder.</i>

795
00:58:56,792 --> 00:58:58,792
<i>How did you find it?</i>

796
00:58:58,792 --> 00:59:00,517
<i>We need to find out everything
about that bastard.</i>

797
00:59:00,517 --> 00:59:02,190
<i>That way, we can at least try to stop him.</i>

798
00:59:02,190 --> 00:59:04,360
<i>The version of us...</i>

799
00:59:04,360 --> 00:59:05,920
<i>that we've lost.</i>

800
00:59:06,539 --> 00:59:10,232
<i>For the protagonist to have
a strong motivation to travel back in time,</i>

801
00:59:11,599 --> 00:59:14,056
<i>someone would have to die.</i>

802
00:59:14,056 --> 00:59:16,576
<i>This is the only way to avert that fate.</i>

803
00:59:17,206 --> 00:59:18,906
<i>I need to stop.</i>
